{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And they called.</b> He mentioned above the miracles done with the manna, and now returns to tell its praise:" "Some say: like gad seed, white coriander, called in Arabic kasbīr. Others say: mustard. I do not know, for it has no parallel in Scripture except regarding the manna. Likewise צפיחית. The Gaon [Saadia] said it is רקיק מצות. Now when eaten as it descended, it is like צפיחית in honey; if cooked, its taste is like cream of oil. These two flavors Scripture showed us."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {1 "כוסברתא is Aramaic for coriander; rendered as transliteration since it is the term under discussion. צפיחית and רקיק מצות left in Hebrew as they are the specific words being glossed."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:14.171924872Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}